<title>JAPAN: Siemens to start selling DRAM chips in Japan - paper.</title>
<headline>Siemens to start selling DRAM chips in Japan - paper.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Siemens AG will enter Japan's dynamic random access memory (DRAM) chip market after increasing its stake in a joint venture with Fuji Electric Co Ltd earlier this year, a Japanese newspaper said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Siemens will import Siemens-made DRAM chips from Europe from next year, the Nihon Keizai Shimbun economic daily said. Siemens spent several hundred million yen in July to increase its stake in Fuji Electronic Components Ltd to 80 percent from 50 percent, the paper said.</p>
<p>Spokesmen for the companies were not immediately available for comment.</p>
</text>
